  "conclusion": "Failed open-ended EEM repeatedly leaves bank0/SID0 pending while the registered bank1 fault handler sees no pending fault. Both banks were clear before bind. Linux disables the shared IRQ as unhandled.",
  "limits": [
    "Pending peer evidence does not prove the initiating transaction, cause of every transfer stall or permission to ACK/reset bank0.",
    "Snapshots are sampled before bind and in the final capture; no precise fault onset timing claim.",
    "Bank0 node/driver remains disabled; all registers sampled passively with a get-if-active/noidle PM reference on the same powered bank1 domain. No DMA/IOVA addresses read.",
    "Diagnostic success is separate from EEM data failure. Complete host/all18CPU captures and authenticated physical recovery required."
  ]
